00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:51.300
in Massachusetts who asked,

452
00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:55.680
When the power goes out in the office, since you guys work on a sound stage,

453
00:23:55.980 --> 00:23:58.900
how did the whole process of making the lights go out work?

454
00:23:58.920 --> 00:24:01.020
Was it simple or did it take a lot of planning?

455
00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:03.560
Ryan, thank you for this question.

456
00:24:03.780 --> 00:24:06.780
This is a kind of like nerdy production question I like.

457
00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:14.640
Per Randy Cordray, our lighting and electric crew, who was headed up by our gaffer Frank Esposito

458
00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:18.640
and his best boy Jim Holt, had to do a lot of work to make this happen.

459
00:24:19.260 --> 00:24:24.640
Because as Randy pointed out, all of the interior lights in the office go out,

460
00:24:24.760 --> 00:24:31.780
but the exterior lights that light up our fakie scrim, you know, to the fake outside,

461
00:24:31.780 --> 00:24:34.300
outside, out the windows, those all stay on.

462
00:24:34.560 --> 00:24:37.340
So we couldn't just like throw the master switch.

463
00:24:37.640 --> 00:24:37.840
Right.

464
00:24:38.540 --> 00:24:41.020
Some had to stay on, some had to go off.

465
00:24:41.340 --> 00:24:48.780
But also, all of our stage lights in like various support rooms around the sound stage,

466
00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:51.820
like craft service and the sound booth and all of that,

467
00:24:52.020 --> 00:24:55.360
they're all on this same like lighting board.

468
00:24:55.780 --> 00:24:56.340
Right.

469
00:24:56.460 --> 00:24:57.600
And they can't lose lights.

470
00:24:57.600 --> 00:24:59.540
Our sound booth can't lose lights.

471
00:24:59.540 --> 00:25:00.040
Yeah.

472
00:25:00.320 --> 00:25:05.040
So what they did was they ganged, I guess that's a term, or combined,

473
00:25:05.260 --> 00:25:08.740
all of the circuits that needed to go dark into a single dimmer.

474
00:25:09.060 --> 00:25:12.440
And then they would give a cue to our first AD to hit that dimmer.

475
00:25:12.520 --> 00:25:15.700
And then the appropriate lights would go off and the others would stay on.

476
00:25:16.180 --> 00:25:17.060
